.TH LINUX-MOUNT-AUDITOR 1 "September 2026" "linux-mount-auditor 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
linux-mount-auditor \- inspect Linux mount configuration without changing it
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B linux-mount-auditor
.I COMMAND
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.RI [ TARGET ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Parses /proc/self/mountinfo and optionally /etc/fstab. Results describe only the mount namespace visible to the process and are not an atomic snapshot. No mount, filesystem, device, service, swap, namespace, or configuration state is modified.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B inspect
List current mounts.
.TP
.B tree
Render the mount-ID hierarchy.
.TP
.BI show " TARGET"
Show the longest lexical mount-point match. Symlinks are not resolved.
.TP
.B fstab
Show persistent configuration records, including swap.
.TP
.B compare
Conservatively compare fstab with current visible mounts.
.TP
.B audit
Show contextual and review findings.
.TP
.B check
As audit, but exit 1 when warning-level findings exist.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --json
Emit stable schema-version-1 JSON to stdout.
.TP
.B --all
Include all mounts and bypass filters.
.TP
.B --include-pseudo
Include pseudo and RAM-backed mounts.
.TP
.BI --type " TYPE"
Filter by exact filesystem type.
.TP
.BI --source " SOURCE"
Filter by exact source.
.TP
.BI --target " TARGET"
Filter by exact target, or provide show's target.
.TP
.BI --fstab " PATH"
Read an alternate fstab fixture read-only.
.TP
.BI --mountinfo " PATH"
Read an alternate mountinfo fixture read-only.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 success; 1 check finding or no show match; 2 usage; 3 required data unavailable; 4 malformed or partial data; 5 internal/resource error.
.SH PRIVACY
Output can reveal usernames, paths, container IDs, server/share names, and storage identifiers. No data is persisted or transmitted by the program.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fstab (5),
.BR proc (5),
.BR mount_namespaces (7)
